 catch zone {x8, x8+dx8} (the game accepts either `ball_x == pos` or `new_x == pos`). It stops at the nearest edge of the zone, so a sticky‑action overshoot still lands inside the zone.\n\nHidden layer 1 (8 units, s = 6, gate scale M = 100). Four direction classes — Down‑Right, Down‑Left, Up‑Right, Up‑Left — are detected with exact linear gates built from the ball/trail one‑hots: horizontal gate = (ball col + [x=0]) − trail col − 1 (0 iff moving right, incl. the pause at the left wall), and vertical gates A(ball row)+B(trail row) that are 0 for \"down\" (dy=+1, or dy=0 at rows 0/2/4 after a brick/top‑wall bounce) resp. \"up\" (dy=−1, or dy=0 at row 8 after a paddle hit) and ≤ −1 otherwise. For each class k, unit a_k = tanh(6·(L_k(ball cell) − paddle col − 0.5) + 100·gate_k) is +1 exactly when the class is active and the paddle is left of the zone (L_k = zone's left edge, a per‑cell table), else −1; unit b_k = tanh(6·(R_k − paddle col + 0.5) − 100·gate_k) is −1 exactly when the paddle is right of the zone, else +1. Paddle column enters as −6·col from channel 0.\n\nLayer 2: unit 0 = tanh(3·Σa + 9) ≈ +1 iff \"move right\" needed; unit 1 = tanh(−3·Σb + 9) ≈ +1 iff \"move left\" needed. Output: right = 8·h0, left = 8·h1, no‑op = −4·(h0+h1); up/down/fire get bias −20.\n\n```edits\n# ---------- biases layer 1 ----------\nb1[0:4] = -103\nb1[4:8] = 103\n# ---------- paddle (channel 0, row 9) -> -6*col, all 8 units ----------\nW1[540:600:6, 0] = [0,-6,-12,-18,-24,-30,-36,-42,-48,-54]\nW1[540:600:6, 1] = [0,-6,-12,-18,-24,-30,-36,-42,-48,-54]\nW1[540:600:6, 2] = [0,-6,-12,-18,-24,-30,-36,-42,-48,-54]\nW1[540:600:6, 3] = [0,-6,-12,-18,-24,-30,-36,-42,-48,-54]\nW1[540:600:6, 4] = [0,-6,-12,-18,-24,-30,-36,-42,-48,-54]\nW1[540:600:6, 5] = [0,-6,-12,-18,-24,-30,-36,-42,-48,-54]\nW1[540:600:6, 6] = [0,-6,-12,-18,-24,-30,-36,-42,-48,-54]\nW1[540:600:6, 7] = [0,-6,-12,-18,-24,-30,-36,-42,-48,-54]\n# ---------- unit 0: a_DR, ball (channel 3) ----------\nW1[3:60:6, 0] = [148,154,248,34